[[2047,15,33554432,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The optional services relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J60 controls\nthe heating circuit for the seats as well as the electric rear windows\nand sun roof: \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 See\n\t\tE3060\n\t\tSUN ROOF\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 , \n\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 See\n\t\tE3051\n\t\tELECTRIC REAR WINDOWS\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 , \n\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 See\n\t\tE3075\n\t\tHEATED SEATS\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 ).</strong></p><p>The coil for relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J60 is energized when\nthe ignition is switched on (INT/A) by the line for fuse F6 of supplementary\nfuse box B98 B, whilst the supply at the relay contact arrives from\nthe battery, through the line for maxifuse J/B2 of B99.</strong></p><p>This supply passes through fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which\nguarantees the protection of the circuit and reaches the switch\non the seat via the connection \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>D70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              : the supply for the device\nis therefore controlled by the ignition (INT/A); and is also connected\nto earth \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>C20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>When the switch on the seat is pressed,\ncommand signals (positive and negative) are sent to the motor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N38</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              :\nreversing the signals according to the contact which is closed determines\nthe direction of the rotation of the actual motor.</p>"]]